I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP capability to write the log line or call the metadata service. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond its declared grants. The metadata call would also send the user's question to an external host. The code below implements only the node's contract.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{conversation-context, response-result};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/tool-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(ctx: conversation-context) -> response-result;
}
```

